use std
into ios.amni

Imports os (no namespace prefix needed beyond `os::`). A command-line packager that turns a Helium program into an iOS app project and, given a Mac reachable over ssh, builds it there or hands it to a release script for TestFlight. It mirrors tools/mobile/android.sh. Every step runs one shell command through `os::run_command`; paths go into commands inside single quotes. On the Mac, commands run from the login home and put /opt/homebrew/bin first on PATH; B, the Mac build folder, is "build/helium-ios". For an SDL version v, the Mac SDL folder S is B followed by "/sdl-" and v (the text of v, never a literal "v").

`Opts` holds the text fields main, name, id, assets, icons, ver, team, out, mac, release, root, hcn and sdl, the flag portrait and the flag ok.

`env_or(name, dflt)` is the value `os::env` reads for name when it finds one that is not empty, else dflt (no shell, no temporary files).

`abs_path(p)` is p when it starts with a slash, else the PWD environment value, a slash and p.

`dir_of(p)` is the text before the last slash of p, or "." when p has no slash; `base_of(p)` is the text after the last slash, or all of p.

`fill(t, key, value)` returns a copy of t with every occurrence of key replaced by value.

`sh(step, cmd)` prints "ios: " followed by step, runs cmd with `os::run_command` and returns true when it exits with 0; otherwise it writes "ios: " followed by step and " failed" and a newline through `os::write_stderr` and returns false.

`opts_of()` reads the command line into an `Opts`. ver starts as "1.0.0", out as `abs_path` of "dist-ios", team as `env_or`("APPLE_TEAM_ID", ""), and ok as true. When there are fewer than 2 arguments ok is false. Argument 1 is main (through `abs_path`). Then from argument 2 on: "--name", "--id", "--ver", "--team", "--mac" and "--release" take the next argument as name, id, ver, team, mac and release; "--assets", "--icons" and "--out" take the next argument through `abs_path` as assets, icons and out; "--portrait" sets portrait. An option that needs a value at the end of the line, or any other argument, makes ok false. ok is also false when name or id is empty. root is `env_or`("HELIUM_ROOT", x) where x is `dir_of` applied four times to `abs_path` of argument 0 (the program is root/tools/mobile/out/ios). hcn is `env_or`("HCN", root followed by "/build/hcn"). sdl is `env_or`("GOOSE_GFX", the HOME environment value followed by "/.goose/pkg/github.com/aardappel/goose_gfx/v1") followed by "/third_party/SDL".

`sdl_version(sdl)` reads sdl followed by "/include/SDL3/SDL_version.h" and returns the values of its "#define SDL_MAJOR_VERSION", "#define SDL_MINOR_VERSION" and "#define SDL_MICRO_VERSION" lines (the text after the name, spaces trimmed) joined with dots; it returns "" when the file cannot be read or a line is missing.

`project_yml(o)` reads o.root followed by "/tools/mobile/ios/project.yml.in" (returning "" when it cannot) and fills "@NAME@" with name, "@ID@" with id, "@PREFIX@" with the id up to its last dot, "@TEAM@" with team, "@VER@" with ver, and "@ORIENT@" with "[UIInterfaceOrientationPortrait]" when portrait is set, else "[UIInterfaceOrientationLandscapeLeft, UIInterfaceOrientationLandscapeRight]".

`stage(o)` builds the Xcode project folder W, which is o.out, a slash and o.id, and returns W, or "" when a step fails. Steps, each through `sh`: "staging" removes W and makes W/src, W/assets and W/app; "compiling" runs, inside the folder of o.main, HC_LIB set to o.root followed by "/hc/lib" and then o.hcn with the file name of o.main, W/src/main.c and "--static"; "runtime" copies o.root/hc/hrt.h and o.root/tools/mobile/ios/helium_ios.c into W/src; when assets is not empty "assets" copies the contents of assets (cp -R of assets followed by "/.") into W/assets; when icons is not empty "icons" copies icons as W/app/Assets.xcassets. Last it writes `project_yml(o)` to W/project.yml (an empty template or a failed write prints "ios: project.yml failed" and returns "").

`mac_sdl(o, v)` makes sure the Mac has a static SDL for iPhone at S/libs-iphoneos/libSDL3.a and returns whether it does. When ssh to o.mac finds that file already (test -f) it returns true at once. Otherwise "SDL source" rsyncs (archive mode, with --delete, excluding .git, test and android-project) the folder o.sdl to o.mac at S/src, and "SDL build" runs over ssh, inside S: cmake -S src -B b-iphoneos -G Ninja with -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=iOS -DCMAKE_OSX_SYSROOT=iphoneos -DCMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES=arm64 -DCMAKE_OSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=16.0 -DSDL_SHARED=OFF -DSDL_STATIC=ON -DSDL_TEST_LIBRARY=OFF -DSDL_TESTS=OFF -DSDL_EXAMPLES=OFF -DSDL_CAMERA=OFF -DSDL_RENDER=OFF -DSDL_OPENGL=OFF -DSDL_OPENGLES=OFF, then nice -n 10 cmake --build b-iphoneos -j 4, then mkdir -p libs-iphoneos and a copy of b-iphoneos/libSDL3.a into it.

`mac_build(o, w)` sends the staged folder w to o.mac and builds it. v is `sdl_version(o.sdl)`; when empty it prints "ios: no SDL source at " and o.sdl and returns false. Then `mac_sdl`, then "upload" rsyncs (archive mode, --delete, excluding build, sdl and *.xcodeproj) w followed by a slash to o.mac at B/id followed by a slash, then "project" runs over ssh, inside B/id: ln -s -f -n with "../sdl-" followed by v as the target and sdl as the link name, then xcodegen generate -q. When release is not empty, "release" runs over ssh nice -n 10 ~/build/amni-ios-release/release.sh with release as its argument, and on success prints "ios: " followed by name and " sent to TestFlight". Otherwise "build" runs over ssh, inside B/id, nice -n 10 xcodebuild build -project name.xcodeproj -scheme name -destination generic/platform=iOS -configuration Release -derivedDataPath build/dd CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO -quiet, and on success prints "ios: built B/id/build/dd/Build/Products/Release-iphoneos/" followed by name, ".app (unsigned) on " and mac. Returns whether every step passed.

`main()` reads `opts_of()`. When ok is false it prints "usage: ios MAIN.amni --name NAME --id com.example.app [--assets DIR] [--icons DIR.xcassets] [--ver 1.0.0] [--team TEAMID] [--out DIR] [--portrait] [--mac HOST [--release CASE]]" and stops. Then w is `stage`; when empty it stops. When mac is empty it prints "ios: staged " followed by w and " (run with --mac HOST to build it on a Mac with Xcode, xcodegen, cmake and ninja)" and stops; otherwise it runs `mac_build`.
